---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeadlineMotion from "../components/HeadlineMotion.astro";
import CallActions from "../components/CallActions.astro";
import { PHONE_DISPLAY, TEL_URL } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Yardulum Founders Club"
  description="Every landscaping company that takes part while we build Yardulum joins the Founders Club and keeps founder pricing for life, locked for as long as they stay subscribed. Setup and sales training in person."
>
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Yardulum · In development</p>
      <h1>
        <HeadlineMotion effect="rise" lines={["The Founders Club."]} />
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every landscaping company that takes part while we build Yardulum joins
        the Founders Club. Members keep founder pricing for life: the monthly
        price you join at stays locked for as long as you stay subscribed.
      </p>
      <CallActions />
    </header>
    <div class="club-grid">
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="get-heading">
        <h2 id="get-heading">What you get</h2>
        <ul class="benefits">
          <li>
            <strong>Founder pricing for life</strong>, locked at the monthly
            price you join at for as long as you stay subscribed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Setup at your shop.</strong> Charles comes to you and sets
            you up in person.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your price list, built with you.</strong> Charles builds it
            with you now and loads it into Yardulum as that part is ready.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sales training, in person.</strong> For you and whoever
            sells for you: how to walk a customer through an itemized design at
            the kitchen table.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Each piece as it’s ready.</strong> You try every part first,
            starting with the property model.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A direct line.</strong> Call or text Charles at{" "}
            <a href={TEL_URL} set:text={PHONE_DISPLAY} />.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="ask-heading">
        <h2 id="ask-heading">What we ask</h2>
        <ul class="benefits">
          <li>
            Show Charles how you price a job today. One quote that went well and
            one that went sideways is plenty.
          </li>
          <li>
            About 30 minutes every two weeks to tell us what works and what
            doesn’t.
          </li>
          <li>One ride-along on a sales visit, with your customer’s OK.</li>
          <li>Straight answers. If something is wrong or slow, say so.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="for-heading">
      <h2 id="for-heading">Who it’s for</h2>
      <p>
        Landscaping companies in Northeast Ohio that sell install work: beds,
        plantings, sod, patios and walls. Kent, Akron, Cleveland, Canton,
        Youngstown and the towns between.
      </p>
      <p>
        Charles sets up each company himself, so he takes on a few at a time.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="stands-heading">
      <h2 id="stands-heading">Where it stands</h2>
      <p>
        Yardulum is in development. Today we can build a 3D model of a property
        from public mapping data and measure on it, and Charles will show you.
        Designing, pricing and the proposal are being built now.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/#where-it-stands">
        See what works today <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading">Questions</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <p>
          Yardulum will be a monthly subscription. Charles goes over the price
          with you in person and gives you the terms in writing before you pay
          anything. Members keep founder pricing for life: the price stays
          locked for as long as you stay subscribed.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why join before it’s finished?</summary>
        <p>
          You lock in the founder price, and Yardulum gets built around how you
          actually sell. Charles would rather hear what’s wrong from you now
          than after it’s done.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How far will Charles drive?</summary>
        <p>Anywhere in Northeast Ohio. If you’re farther out, call anyway.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="join-heading">
      <h2 id="join-heading">Ask about joining</h2>
      <ol class="join">
        <li>Call or text Charles at {PHONE_DISPLAY}.</li>
        <li>
          He comes to your shop, hears how you price jobs now and shows you the
          property model.
        </li>
        <li>If it’s a fit, you get the terms in writing before you decide.</li>
      </ol>
      <CallActions />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .club-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--s12);
  }
  .benefits,
  .join {
    margin: var(--s4) 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .benefits li,
  .join li {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }
  .benefits strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .club-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
